{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.422, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2327}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2327, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8613, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 947, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 442}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01S66bjmw2xQ1jzp17Mxpsvm", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different likelihood-ratio thresholds and profile over different nuisance parameters. The dSph gamma-ray limit is a one-sided 95% upper limit defined by a TS drop of 2.71 (a drop of 1.355 in ln L) from the maximum of the likelihood. It profiles over each dwarf's J-factor, through a Gaussian prior on log10 of the J normalization s, with log10 s in [-3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = -2 ln L. The paper calls 3.84 the nominal 95% interval threshold for one parameter of interest and notes that it differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred on 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T081855Z_dev-02_staged_2ba7", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different likelihood-ratio thresholds and profile over different nuisance parameters. The dSph gamma-ray limit is a one-sided 95% upper limit defined by a TS drop of 2.71 (a drop of 1.355 in ln L) from the maximum of the likelihood. It profiles over each dwarf's J-factor, through a Gaussian prior on log10 of the J normalization s, with log10 s in [-3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = -2 ln L. The paper calls 3.84 the nominal 95% interval threshold for one parameter of interest and notes that it differs from the one-sided 2.71 prescription. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centred on 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 10.654, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19377, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1271, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 10940, "cache_read_input_tokens": 14431, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:19:06+00:00"}
